{"title":"Career Roadmap · Rehabilitation Technician","role":"Rehabilitation Technician","summary":"A Rehabilitation Technician supports rehabilitation professionals in helping patients improve mobility, functional independence, safety, and participation in daily activities. In a Prosthetics & Orthotics pathway, the role may involve assisting with the fabrication, fitting, adjustment, maintenance, and functional use of prosthetic and orthotic devices under the direction of appropriately qualified professionals.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Prosthetics & Orthotics"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Rehabilitation Technician supports rehabilitation professionals in helping patients improve mobility, functional independence, safety, and participation in daily activities. In a Prosthetics & Orthotics pathway, the role may involve assisting with the fabrication, fitting, adjustment, maintenance, and functional use of prosthetic and orthotic devices under the direction of appropriately qualified professionals."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical work environments include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Prosthetics & orthotics clinics"},{"text":"Rehabilitation hospitals"},{"text":"Orthopaedic hospitals"},{"text":"Physical medicine and rehabilitation departments"},{"text":"Mobility and assistive-device centres"},{"text":"Paediatric rehabilitation centres"},{"text":"Community rehabilitation programmes"},{"text":"Prosthetic/orthotic manufacturing facilities"},{"text":"Home and community rehabilitation services"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Qualification and scope note","text":"“Rehabilitation Technician” is a broad job title. The exact eligibility, registration requirements, permitted clinical responsibilities, and supervision requirements vary by country, state, employer, and profession. A generic B.Sc/BPT/BOT/BMLT degree should not automatically be treated as equivalent to a recognized Prosthetics & Orthotics professional qualification. Students specifically targeting prosthetic/orthotic clinical practice should verify the qualification and registration pathway applicable to the intended role."}]},{"heading":"Recommended Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"UG / Allied Health Foundation"},{"type":"flow","items":["Anatomy","Physiology","Rehabilitation Fundamentals"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Prosthetics & Orthotics-Specific Training"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical / Workshop Internship"},{"type":"h","text":"Rehabilitation Technician / P&O Technician"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Rehabilitation / P&O Technician"},{"type":"h","text":"Specialized Technician / Workshop Supervisor"},{"type":"h","text":"Rehabilitation Technology / P&O Operations / Clinical Support"},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced Qualification / Management / Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["The strongest candidates combine clinical understanding","device technology","fabrication skills","patient interaction","documentation."],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career Stage","Typical Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"UG Student"},{"text":"Anatomy, biomechanics, rehabilitation fundamentals"}],[{"text":"Trainee"},{"text":"Workshop and clinical exposure"}],[{"text":"Entry Level"},{"text":"Device preparation, fitting support, maintenance and patient assistance"}],[{"text":"Experienced Technician"},{"text":"Independent technical tasks within authorized scope"}],[{"text":"Senior Technician"},{"text":"Complex device support and quality control"}],[{"text":"Specialist"},{"text":"Paediatric, sports, neuro-rehabilitation, advanced mobility devices"}],[{"text":"Supervisor"},{"text":"Workshop/team coordination and quality management"}],[{"text":"Advanced Professional"},{"text":"Rehabilitation technology, clinical research, product development or management"}